CCAT — translating the cluster requirement into a survey
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The planned DSFG / CIB-Mid pilot covers 100 deg^2.  Cluster surface densities for
  a benchmark-class halo (M_500 = 1e15, i.e. the very top of the mass function) are of
  order 0.01-0.05 per deg^2 out to z ~ 1, so such a field contains only a few.  The
  requirement below should therefore be read as 'how much sky, at what mass floor',
  not as 'how many pointings'.

  N required (clustering-inflated, u >= 3 sigma_c) = 7.608e+03 benchmark clusters at r < 1.5 theta_500.
    at 0.05 such clusters per deg^2 (optimistic): 1.522e+05 deg^2 of sky
    at 0.01 such clusters per deg^2 (conservative): 7.608e+05 deg^2 of sky
    NOTE Delta_xi scales roughly as <ln mu>, and <ln mu> falls as M^(2/3)-ish, so a
    sample of lower-mass clusters needs more of them than the surface-density scaling
    alone suggests.  Use this as an order of magnitude.

  Cross-experiment comparison is the point of the common benchmark:
  run all three scripts and compare the 'BEST CONFIGURATION' lines.

